Subject: [PATCH] [Backport] CVE-2026-121174 (2/2) and CVE-2026-121107

Manual cherry-pick of patch originally reviewed on
https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8125729:
Address various Background Fetch CORS issues

This CL expands test coverage and fixes lingering response type and
header exposure bugs resolved by moving Background Fetch away from
RequestMode::kNavigate to standard RequestMode::kCors enforcement, and
expands test coverage.

Specifically:

- Fixes response type assignment in
  MarkRequestCompleteTask::StoreResponse by dynamically assigning
  FetchResponseType::kCors when the response URL origin differs from
  the registration's initiator origin (instead of hardcoding
  kDefault). This ensures JavaScript Response objects enforce
  strict CORS exposed-header filtering (Access-Control-Expose-Headers)
  and correctly mark response types as 'cors'.
- Adds browser tests verifying CORS restrictions across redirect
  chains (FailsOnCrossOriginRedirectWithoutCorsHeaders,
  SucceedsOnCrossOriginRedirectWithCorsHeaders).
- Adds browser tests verifying CORS OPTIONS preflight blocking on
  custom request headers (FailsWithCustomHeaderWithoutPreflight).
- Adds browser tests verifying accurate credentials mode plumbing and
  wildcard origin constraints
  (FailsWithCredentialsIncludeAgainstWildcardOrigin,
  SucceedsWithCredentialsOmitAgainstWildcardOrigin).
- Adds browser tests verifying JavaScript response record encapsulation
  (CrossOriginResponseTypeIsCors, NonCorsExposedHeaderNotExposed).
- Introduces standardized Web Platform Test (WPT) suite under
  external/wpt/background-fetch/cors.https.window.js verifying
  interoperable CORS behaviors (preflights, response types, exposed
  headers, credentials).

